Objective:
Current status:
Input artifacts:
Files changed:
Files not to touch:
Known issues:
Required checks:
Next recommended action:
```


--- brief ---
You are a bounded implementation worker, not an auditor. Follow the primary design and fix only your assigned defects. No subagents, no lifecycle commands, no context refresh, no installs/restarts, no commits, no ACL or sandbox changes. Do not modify checksums, VERSION, release registrations or unrelated files. Primary owns integration and all PF transitions.
Use targeted rg/AST reads: Serena has no configured languages. Do not dump tools/processforge.py or scan all .pf. Aim for <= 20 focused tool calls; before code edits use at most 8 reads, each <= 180 lines. Write a failing regression from the supplied defect evidence, make the minimal repair, then run focused tests. On the FIRST sandbox PermissionError stop trying environment workarounds; preserve runnable tests and tell primary the exact command. You can still implement and perform static reasoning. No repeated broad exploration. Finish promptly with a concise report (<= 100 lines), exact changed files, actual test results vs unexecuted checks, risks. Use repo-relative paths in the report and describe absolute-path samples in words. Public tests use disposable temp fixtures, neutral names, no this-machine paths. Write report even on blockers.


Fix A05. In core_update.py workplace_migration_plan currently accepts copy_if_missing source absent from ZIP; archive.read KeyError in apply leaves journal applying. Validate archive source declarations (missing, directory, invalid path) during planning BEFORE target mutations; keep optional/already-present semantics justified by contract. Apply must fail with structured status and recoverable journal/backup if an archive/read/extraction failure still occurs after planning (test fault at apply boundary). Do not swallow programmer errors broadly. Read audit native-core/audit_core_update_missing_migration_source.py and smoke_core_update_manifest.py, local docs update/migration contract. Real minimal ZIP regression: malformed manifest missing member plan blocked, no target change, positive migration passes and existing target preserved. Test post-plan read fault journal not applying. Do not operate installed distribution/workplace or bump versions.

